roper size, making these \"premium\" headphones look like a budget knock off. Noise cancelation is a complete joke and barely works at all. Sony does not let you adjust the anc levels manually, so you're stuck with whatever it thinks you want to hear, which apparently is everything around you. These (literally) cannot even filter out a simple white noise machine or the sound of fans blowing. Yes, I turned off the motion based \"adaptive\" mode too. Touch controls are sporadic and occasionally trigger on their own. Sound quality is muddy and flat, even after EQ adjustments in the app. Speaking of which, these headphones and the accompanying app are incredibly intrusive, asking for accounts and permissions at just about every step in the setup process. Ive never seen headphones require so many permissions and location access. I am truly stumped as to how these are so highly reviewed, ive purchased no name brands from auction sites for a fifth of the price that performed way better than these. Even the packaging on these is cheap. Hands down the worst headphones purchase ive ever made, thank goodness for the generous return policy."}]}, "specifications": [{"name": "Connection Type", "value": "Wireless"}, {"name": "Headphone Fit", "value": "Over-the-Ear"}, {"name": "Style", "value": "Pro"}, {"name": "Product Width", "value": "10.40 inches"}, {"name": "Product Length", "value": "12.50 inches"}, {"name": "Warranty - Parts", "value": "1-year limited manufacturer's warranty"}, {"name": "Warranty - Labor", "value": "1-year limited manufacturer's warranty"}], "related_products": [{"position": 1, "product_id": "9647449009722761431", "product_token": "", "title": "Sony WH 1000XM5SA Noise Cancelling Wireless Over Ear Headphones", "link": "https://www.google.com/search?ibp=oshop&q=Sony+WH+1000XM5SA+Noise+Cancelling+Wireless+Over+Ear+Headphones&prds=catalogid:9647449009722761431,gpcid:1753813024263151123,headlineOfferDocid:370997478155054150,imageDocid:7319952843371072245,pvo:2,pv